WEBVTT

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.510
There should be another assault! 
Don't let your guard down!

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:30.780
Izuru!

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.820
What's wrong? Izuru, are you all right?

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.980
This is Red 5. I just... I just...

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.150
What the heck did you just do?!

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.420
What happened?

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.530
I just saw something disturbing.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.510
What?!

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.840
What's that?

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.680
Like what? Was it a ghostie?

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.950
Right! I need to give pursuit.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.450
What gives? Why isn't it moving?

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.390
What's going on, Izuru?

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.390
What did you see?

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.600
During battle, I-

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.170
Red 5, you are prohibited 
from further communication.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.850
You must not tell anyone about 
what you just witnessed.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.260
Upon your return, come 
report to me immediately.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.580
Yes, Ma'am.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.460
Izuru, what happened?!

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.210
Respond, Izuru!

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:30.770
It's working?

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.110
What's wrong with him now?

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.310
Maybe he got an owie?

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.270
His unit may have taken some 
damage, but Izuru is fine.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:47.710
Hey, look!

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.900
All of the enemy vessels are 
pulling out of the battle zone?

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.630
Does that mean we won?

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.550
Yay!

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.170
We won! We won!

00:01:56.870 --> 00:02:00.180
But why? They had victory 
in their grasp...

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:01.480
That was a piece of cake! Yay!

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.400
"Disclosure"

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.010
The entire enemy fleet is retreating!

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.570
We will begin accepting 
injured onto our ship!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.570
What should we do?

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.830
Commence a running fight?

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:57.500
If we could, I would have 
issued the orders already!

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.910
The tactical heavy laser system 
has been damaged beyond repair!

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.090
I am unable to reach the 
squad that was guarding it.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.030
The convoy vessel, Stout, 
is requesting help.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.650
Likewise, the convoy vessel, 
Shiloh, is also requesting help.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.120
We're also receiving distress signals

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.490
from ships in the first and second 
lines of defense that are unable to move.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.320
Earth's GDF Headquarters 
are still on the line.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.110
They would like a 
detailed damage report.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.520
Purple 2 has boarded!

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.950
Both the unit and pilot are unharmed.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.170
Welcome back, Miss. You did wonderful.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.290
Kei!

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.040
Are you okay? Kei!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.170
Hang in there!

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.340
I-I'm sorry...

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.130
Calm down, Kei. The battle is over now.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.180
We're glad to see you made 
it back safe and sound.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.640
Team Rabbits fought valiantly out there.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.260
We're all very proud of you.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:54.270
Now leave the rest to us 
and try to take it easy.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.460
Where is Red 5?

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.270
Has Izuru made it back yet?

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.770
I don't know.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.800
I haven't heard one way or the other.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.400
Did something happen to Red 5?

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.100
Doberman and Rabbits are the

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.240
only squads that didn't 
suffer any casualties.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:18.200
For them to survive that battle 
royal essentially unscathed,

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.920
their units must be something else!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.340
No kiddin'!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.050
We're the ones who assembled these 
puppies and kept them up an' running!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.340
There's no way the 
Wulgaru could touch 'em!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.880
Right. We owe it all to you.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:29.600
Thank you for-

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.260
Ow!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.810
That's not what you should 
be saying, you lame pilot!

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.430
Wha-?!

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.230
Was that the best you could do?!

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.270
Watching you pissed me off!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.490
Well, excuse me!

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:45.900
Man, you suck!

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.700
Next time you're gonna get shot 
down and die if you keep this up!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.740
If that doesn't sit well 
if you, train harder to-

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.960
Hey! Watch what you say!

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.280
But it's all true!

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.200
Let go of me, Papa! Let go, dammit!

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.730
I'm sorry about that 
foul mouth of hers.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.500
There's no reason to hold me back!

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.500
She must have inherited it from my wife.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.870
Just you wait, you...! 
You...! You little...!

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:03.170
Believe it or not, she 
was worried about you.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.710
Please don't hold it against her.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.710
I'll get you, dammit!

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.470
It-it's fine. After all, she's right...

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:10.890
You lame pilot!

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.260
They sure did a number on you!

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.600
But in a way, you were lucky.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.480
If it had gone any deeper, that would 
have been the end of you, Icchan.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:19.770
Icchan?

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:23.610
It doesn't look like your transmission 
cables or drives got damaged.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.570
Are you sure that it suddenly 
stopped responding to your orders?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.780
Yes. When I tried to pursue an 
enemy unit, it wouldn't budge.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.490
Which means it must have 
been the JURIA-SYSTEM.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.120
That's the only explanation 
I can come up with.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:39.790
So the AHSMB tried to defend itself?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.870
Looks like it's gonna take a while

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.070
for you to tame this bunking bronco.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.430
That means I still haven't 
mastered my unit, doesn't it?

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.720
You got into a dogfight 
with the enemy, right?

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:53.760
What was he like?

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.000
Could you see his face?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.990
Or what he looked like?

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.930
Well, uh...

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.150
Okay, okay, stop! That's 
enough chit-chat.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.070
Isn't the captain waiting? 
You'd better run.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.900
R-right!

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.570
Anyway, please take good 
care of my unit for me.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.080
And then the enemy showed himself to me.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.920
I was surprised to see 
that he looked human.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.050
He looked just like that 
lady I met at the pool.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:33.840
At the pool?

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:35.330
Right.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.780
We aren't supposed to 
remember our pasts,

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:40.510
but for some odd reason, 
I remembered her.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:41.770
And then-

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.440
That's enough.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.890
You may not mention this

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:50.360
to anyone henceforth, not even 
the members of Team Rabbits.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.870
I've always found it strange!

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.460
Who was that lady?

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.810
Why is she the only person I remember?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.410
Instructor, do you know what she-

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:04.550
I am no longer your instructor.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.210
I'm your captain.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.120
I will issue further orders later.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:12.020
You may leave.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:12.670
But-

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.800
You are dismissed!

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.730
I need to report to the commander...

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.440
"This duel was amusing."

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.190
"Let us fight again, 
primitive creature!"

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.760
In other words, he has identified 
Red 5 as his target?

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.390
Most likely.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.540
I never expected this to happen...

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.310
Now that it has come to this,

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.610
I believe it is necessary to enlighten 
Team Rabbits of the situation,

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.940
at least to a certain degree.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.850
It is quite likely that the 
Wulgaru will go after them.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.870
We must psychologically prepare 
them for what is to come,

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.830
although I consider 
doing so most cruel...

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.800
Are you worried about that young man?

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:35.900
That is a given.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:40.680
He may have forgotten about 
me, but I still remember him.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:44.350
If only I could see that 
he is indeed well...

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.790
You may go near the 
exam room if you like.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.540
Of course, you will not be permitted 
to speak with him directly.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.290
Why do you always hang out in my room?!

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.960
Go sleep in your own rooms!

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.410
I'm too excited to sleep!

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:21.510
When I'm by myself, I keep 
thinking about that battle.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:25.680
Besides, we can see all of the 
returning ally ships from this room.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.490
We were beaten like dogs, didn't we?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.580
What?! But didn't we win?

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.580
The Wulgaru ran away!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:51.070
I don't know why, but it's true 
that the enemy pulled back.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.270
Regardless, Earth suffered 
far heavier losses.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:57.590
Forty percent...

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.010
...of our forces were 
literally annihilated.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.850
Hey, something smells really good!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.770
I lit an aroma candle.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.810
I heard they can have 
soothing properties.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.190
Yeah?

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.200
I wonder what's keeping Izuru...

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:19.940
I bet quarantine is taking a while.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:23.310
After all, they said his 
cockpit got torn wide open.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:49.380
Can't sleep?

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.190
"Lame pilot."

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:55.520
That's what I got called... 
by a member of my pit crew.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:03.280
If I had done a better 
job issuing orders,

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.870
the battle may have gone better.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:15.020
If someone else had been the leader...

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.210
If it had been him...

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.000
Just maybe, more lives...

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.000
You're overthinking things!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.930
I doubt anyone could have done better.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:31.100
There is no way I could have handled it.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:36.270
Um, I'm not really sure how to put it,

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.590
but I felt like I could 
rely on you back there!

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.740
Those words held a drop of salvation...

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:51.920
He really is taking forever.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:55.260
He's in the exam room, 
right? I'll check on him!

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.130
They probably won't let you in!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.710
I'll check anyway!

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.530
Izuru!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.920
Thank goodness!

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.570
Where have you been? What happened?

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:32.870
Is something the matter?

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.580
Hey, say something!

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:41.500
K-Kei!

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:46.800
S-sorry.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.220
Why...?

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:11.700
Wait!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:12.700
Izuru!

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.290
Why? What is she doing here?

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.870
Please wait! Who are you?

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.510
Let's go back. Please hurry!

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.080
What's going on?

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.890
Izuru, not gonna eat that?

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.830
Huh? Nah, I'm not hungry.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.690
Then I'll take it!

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:06.160
The food is the only thing

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.750
that's leveled up since 
we've moved to this base!

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:08.750
Hey, what's going on?

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.260
Huh? In regard to? It's so good!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.300
That's what I'd like to know!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.720
You two've been acting 
strange since last night.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.220
What the heck happened?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:23.510
They're all dead? That's horrible.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:27.980
I bet it'll take a while 
to regroup our forces.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.860
Looks like we'll be 
abandoning Ceres Base.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:34.570
Apparently the higher-ups have 
absolutely no idea what to do next.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.660
What is going to happen to us?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.320
The big wigs are already pointing 
their fingers at each other.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:44.880
It won't be long before this base 
is overridden with injured soldiers.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.500
If they strike again now...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.310
We wouldn't last a minute.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.930
What's wrong? You look so glum!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.260
It's the lunch lady!

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.140
What are you doing here?

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.930
Did you come after me?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.280
Dang, that's awe-

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:05.050
I got reassigned shortly after you left.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:07.190
They said that this base 
was a bit understaffed.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.430
I know it's been crazy 
since you arrived,

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:14.420
but don't let one lost battle 
get you down in the dumps!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.830
You're the heroes who 
saved Earth, you know.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.440
We're heroes?

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.410
We are?

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:22.830
That's what the news keeps calling you.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.330
Yesterday's battle was a 
huge victory for Earth!

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.470
It says that Team Rabbits 
is a group of young heroes

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:29.690
who magnificently repelled 
the flood of enemy ships!

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:33.550
Really? So we were a big help after all!

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.760
This is just a repeat of last time!

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:40.010
They need to throw out some 
heroes whenever we lose.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:46.100
Like I said, don't look so glum!

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.620
Come on, Asagi! You ought to eat more.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.570
Want me to bring you seconds?

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.310
No, my stomach is starting 
to hurt again...

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.220
May we join you?

00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:58.620
Uh, sure. Feel free.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.860
Aren't you the operators...?

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:05.680
I am Communications Manager 
Siegfried von Westernach.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.980
I'm Guiliano Visconti.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.170
Hey, where is my milk?

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:11.840
Oh, sorry!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.420
R-right! Just one moment please.

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:16.510
I can't handle second tier studs!

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:19.090
Excuse me for being third tier!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.180
Sorry for interrupting your meal.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.030
We always talk over the monitor,

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:26.100
so we were hoping to 
speak with you in person.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:31.980
Okay! I love octopus and squid, 
especially their pickled innards!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.860
How long do you expect it to 
take to reorganize the fleet?

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.390
I couldn't say.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.160
As it stands now, we don't even know

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.540
the exact scale of our losses.

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:42.090
But not all of the news is bad!

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:43.860
We learned that your AHSMB

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.580
units are able to fight 
on par with the enemy.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:51.090
I imagine we'll build upon your 
AHSMB team and regroup around that.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.880
But if you flip it around,

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.700
the AHSMB units were the only 
thing doing any damage, right?

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:56.960
Now, now.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.720
They should already be working on 
increasing AHSMB unit production.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.350
Although even we aren't 
privy to the details.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.020
Tamaki, this is important! 
Are you paying attention?

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.020
I-I can't pick one at 
the drop of a hat!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:11.280
I can't, I can't, I can't! I just can't!

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.860
You've got your hands full, don't you?

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:14.780
Huh?

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.570
How about I treat everyone to dessert?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.700
Please order anything you like!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.620
Then I'll take a space-sized 
Star Rose Parfait!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.040
FRUIT PARFAIT: LIMITED TIME ONLY 
STAR ROSE PARFAIT: SPACE SIZE

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.290
That was fast...

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.590
Everyone from Team Rabbits!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.510
I've got a message 
from Captain Suzukaze!

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.220
For all of us?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.850
Eh?! But I was just 
about to have dessert!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.430
She needs you pronto!

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:49.600
Team Rabbits is to meet in 
Operating Room No. 7 immediately.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.020
That's all!

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.690
At ease!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:08.310
As you are aware, the GDF suffered 
heavy losses in the Battle of Ceres.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.990
Henceforth, I imagine the AHSMB 
teams, starting with Team Rabbits,

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:13.590
will be sent on an increasing 
number of missions.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.050
In preparation for the upcoming battles,

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.510
I have decided to divulge certain 
information with you in advance.

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:24.420
However, everything said here is of 
the utmost confidential of nature.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:26.930
If you tell anyone...

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.100
We'll meet the firing squad?!

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:35.360
I'll start with this video.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.860
Wasn't I supposed to keep this a secret?

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:43.030
We'll go over it in a bit.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.660
What the heck? We're fighting humans?

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.500
He's saying something to Izuru...!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.570
He isn't human.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:55.460
He may resemble us, but he is 
a completely different species.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:57.880
He looks damn nasty!

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:59.880
Really? I think he's cool.

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:02.420
He's the enemy! The enemy!

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:04.800
Do you like anyone that looks cool?

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.890
I wouldn't say that...

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.440
But you might be right!

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.270
Is this what you were referring to?

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.360
It's not just his appearance.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.860
His fighter moves a lot 
like our AHSMB units.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:29.290
Exactly! Our AHSMBs 
utilize their technology.

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:34.810
Once, two pieces of information were 
leaked through a certain route.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.380
The first was that the Wulgaru 
were preparing to invade Earth.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:41.450
The second was the basic technology 
behind the AHSMB units.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.630
That was the intel.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.920
The AHSMBs that Team Rabbits currently

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.990
pilot were developed using 
that leaked technology.

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.350
So we've been piloting Wulgaru fighters?

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:58.400
Their basic plans may hail 
from Wulgaru origins,

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.310
but we are the ones who adapted 
them for human pilots.

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:05.240
The JURIA-SYSTEM was also developed 
by a member of the MJP.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:12.410
Excuse me...

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:19.380
How did that leaked information 
get to Earth to begin with?

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.110
How did we find out 
that the Wulgaru were

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.840
after Earth and learn 
how the AHSMB work?

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:28.260
A Wulgaru defector delivered 
the information to Earth.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.180
A defector...?

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.950
I will let her explain 
the situation in detail.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.320
It's you...!

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.980
So we meet again.

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:55.950
"The Hunter and the Hunted"
